# STAGE3_CONFIG_APPLIED.diff -- the exact edit that stage 3 is running under.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The run happens in an isolated tree, omni_thr_fit/repo/,
# which is a 2.4 GB working copy and is excluded from the push (see
# scratchpad/sync_stage.sh). So the pushed tree carries FINAL_THRESHOLDS.json --
# what the fit CHOSE -- with no evidence of what the run actually LOADED. Those
# are the same nine numbers only if the edit landed, and "the config was updated"
# is precisely the kind of claim that is assumed rather than checked.
#
# preflight_stage3.sh asserts the equality at launch (assertion 1: it imports
# config.py and compares to FINAL_THRESHOLDS.json, failing on any mismatch), and
# this diff is that assertion's paper trail: config.py.bak_20260831_020934 ->
# config.py, generated with `diff -u`, nothing hand-edited.
#
# Note what is NOT here. task_gate_modes and task_refractory_s are untouched --
# they are inherited from the vision-only fit and were never refitted, which is a
# stated limitation (RUNBOOK sec.2: the three knobs are coupled, so inheriting two
# of them bounds what the third can be claimed to show).
